pageType: content
background:
  type: solid
  color: "$background"
elements:
  - elementId: badge
    elementType: text
    bounds: [60, 40, 300, 20]
    content:
      style: "$badge"
      align: [left, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p>BACKGROUND</p>
  - elementId: title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [60, 65, 700, 40]
    content:
      style: "$pageTitle"
      align: [left, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p><strong>What is an Alpha Factor?</strong></p>
  - elementId: divider
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [60, 115, 1160, 0]
    shapeName: straightConnector1
    border:
      style: solid
      width: 1
      color: "$midGray"
  - elementId: left-card-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [60, 135, 560, 240]
    shapeName: roundRect
    adjustments: [3000]
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$lightGray"
  - elementId: left-card-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [80, 145, 520, 30]
    content:
      fontSize: 18
      color: "$primary"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [left, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p><strong>Definition (Plain Language)</strong></p>
  - elementId: left-card-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [80, 180, 520, 180]
    content:
      style: "$body"
      fontSize: 16
      lineHeight: 1.5
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>An <strong>alpha factor</strong> is a scoring rule that assigns every asset a number at every point in time.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:8px">Higher-scored assets should <em>subsequently outperform</em> lower-scored ones.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:8px">The prediction is about <strong>relative</strong> ranking within a fixed universe — not about absolute price levels.</p>
  - elementId: right-card-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [660, 135, 560, 240]
    shapeName: roundRect
    adjustments: [3000]
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$lightGray"
  - elementId: right-card-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [680, 145, 520, 30]
    content:
      fontSize: 18
      color: "$primary"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [left, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p><strong>Analogy for a Biology Audience</strong></p>
  - elementId: right-card-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [680, 180, 520, 180]
    content:
      style: "$body"
      fontSize: 16
      lineHeight: 1.5
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Think of ranking cells by a gene-expression score, then checking whether the top-ranked cells actually grow faster than the bottom-ranked ones.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:8px">The score is a <strong>signal</strong> extracted from observable data; the forward growth is the <strong>label</strong> we test against.</p>
  - elementId: bottom-card-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [60, 395, 1160, 260]
    shapeName: roundRect
    adjustments: [3000]
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$lightGray"
  - elementId: bottom-card-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [80, 405, 1120, 30]
    content:
      fontSize: 18
      color: "$primary"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [left, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p><strong>Two Key Metrics We Use</strong></p>
  - elementId: metric-ic-icon
    elementType: icon
    bounds: [100, 455, 28, 28]
    iconName: "fas:chart-line"
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$primary"
  - elementId: metric-ic-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [140, 450, 460, 30]
    content:
      fontSize: 18
      color: "$text"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [left, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p><strong>Rank-IC (Information Coefficient)</strong></p>
  - elementId: metric-ic-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [140, 485, 460, 80]
    content:
      fontSize: 16
      color: "$text"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Spearman correlation between today's scores and the forward returns. 1 = perfect ordering, 0 = no skill. Real factors are weak: our best reaches ~0.015.</p>
  - elementId: metric-sharpe-icon
    elementType: icon
    bounds: [660, 455, 28, 28]
    iconName: "fas:scale-balanced"
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$primary"
  - elementId: metric-sharpe-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [700, 450, 460, 30]
    content:
      fontSize: 18
      color: "$text"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [left, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p><strong>Sharpe Ratio</strong></p>
  - elementId: metric-sharpe-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [700, 485, 460, 80]
    content:
      fontSize: 16
      color: "$text"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Evaluates the factor as a trading strategy: buy top-ranked, sell short bottom-ranked. Mean return divided by volatility, annualised.</p>
  - elementId: divider-bottom
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [80, 580, 1120, 0]
    shapeName: straightConnector1
    border:
      style: solid
      width: 1
      color: "$midGray"
  - elementId: insight
    elementType: text
    bounds: [80, 590, 1120, 50]
    content:
      fontSize: 16
      color: "$primary"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        <p><strong>Island factor</strong> = scores from one asset's own history. <strong>Relational factor</strong> = also reads the asset's neighbours in a graph.</p>
  - elementId: footer-bar
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [0, 680, 1280, 40]
    shapeName: rect
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$primary"
  - elementId: footer-left
    elementType: text
    bounds: [60, 685, 600, 30]
    content:
      fontSize: 12
      color: "#FFFFFF"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [left, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p>Relational Alpha Factors · GAT Capstone</p>
  - elementId: footer-right
    elementType: text
    bounds: [1100, 685, 120, 30]
    content:
      fontSize: 12
      color: "#FFFFFF"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [right, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p>3</p>
